# src/config/*.json is deliberately NOT ignored. Those files are generated by
# scripts/sync-config.mjs from devnet.json and target/idl/paritas.json, but
# they are committed anyway, because the Vercel Git integration builds from
# GitHub rather than from an upload: whatever is not in the repository does not
# exist at build time, and target/ is ignored, so the IDL would be missing and
# the build would fail before it started. They are public interface data,
# addresses and an interface description, not secrets. sync-config still
# refreshes them whenever the sources are present, so a local build cannot
# drift; committing them only means a clean clone has something to fall back
# on. The rpcUrl field is stripped on the way in, see sync-config.mjs.
.vercel
.env*
# Incremental typecheck artifact from tsc.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
